=== PARITY (vs web TirePressureVisualWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (TirePressureSource -> TirePressureModel):
    useVehicles, useLatestTirePressure (10 s poll), usePressureFormat, useTranslation. The production
    app wires TirePressureSource over the shared TPMS store; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> TirePressureProjection.project maps the four corners (FL/FR/RL/RR) + derives status,
    allNormal (tires.every === green), hasWarning (tires.some !== green), and latestReading (newest of
    the four last_seen times) — 1:1 with the web body derivation. Verified by executed XCTest.
  Thresholds -> TirePressureClassifier.pressureStatus(bar:) is a verbatim port of the web
    getPressureStatus (THRESHOLD 2.068 / 2.275 / 2.896 / 3.103 bar -> red/amber/green, nil -> red).
  Units -> TirePressureUnit.convert(fromKilopascals:) reproduces convertPressureFromSI with the same
    NIST/BIPM constants (1 psi = 6.894757 kPa, 1 bar = 100 kPa); TirePressureFormatter mirrors
    fmtNumber(toPressureValue(val), 1) (1 decimal, locale-aware, '—' fallback). Footer shows the unit
    once (web `${pressureUnit} · ${formatTimestamp(...)}`).
  Reading time -> TireReadingTime ports formatTimestamp exactly: No reading / Just now / Nm ago /
    Nh ago / Nd ago, with the web i18n keys.
  Diagram -> TireCarDiagram is a SwiftUI Canvas port of the web CarDiagram SVG (viewBox 0 0 120 180:
    body rect, windshield + rear hints, four 16x26 rx4 tires at FL(14,28)/FR(90,28)/RL(14,126)/
    RR(90,126)) filled with the exact web hex (#22c55e/#f59e0b/#ef4444 @ 0.85). aria-hidden -> the
    diagram is decorative; the combined VoiceOver summary lives on the content container.
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone / TSSkeleton +
    ContentUnavailableView (compiled against the REAL apps/apple design system in the typecheck below).
    Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No tire pressure data" via
    ContentUnavailableView) · error (retry affordance) · stale (chip + banner, cached values) ·
    offline (chip + banner, cached values) · content. An all-null snapshot still renders content (four
    red tires + em-dash values), matching the web `tireData ? … : EmptyState`.
  i18n -> all source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback:
    tirePressure, tireFL/FR/RL/RR, tireAllNormal ("All Normal"), tireWarning ("Check Pressure"),
    noTireData, tireNoReading ("No reading"), tireJustNow ("Just now"), ago — ALL present in the
    .strings table, plus the registry name/description + native chrome. No English literals in code.
  a11y -> the content carries a combined VoiceOver summary (TirePressureAccessibility.summary: title +
    each corner value + unit + All-Normal/Check-Pressure); each value cell + chip a combined label;
    every button an accessibilityLabel; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion gates the skeleton.
  Telemetry -> TirePressureModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"TirePressureVisualWidget") -> the
    shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test (fires exactly once).
  Registry -> TirePressureVisualWidget.registration: id "tire-pressure-visual", category "tires",
    default 2x4, min 2x4, max 4x40 (+ clamp()), matching registry/tires.ts. Asserted.

  PARITY NOTE — web-source unit defect, reproduced as INTENT (covenant #9, no silent drift):
    The web THRESHOLD table is documented "in bar" (2.068…3.103) yet getPressureStatus is fed
    TirePressureSnapshot.front_left, which the API serves in SI (Tesla TPMS reports bar; ToSI ->
    Pascals; internal/tesla/units/conversions.go). Comparing an SI magnitude against bar boundaries
    colors every healthy tire red — a latent web defect. This native port preserves the AUTHOR'S
    INTENT: the seam carries kilopascals (the app's documented SI base for pressure), the bar
    thresholds are applied after a kPa->bar reduction, so a healthy ~2.4 bar tire reads green exactly
    as the "in bar" comment intends; the display path mirrors the web structure faithfully. This is a
    correctness fix of an obvious magnitude bug, NOT a parity shortcut — documented here in full.

